{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0325","billNumberShort":"H.B. 325","billNumberLong":"HB0325S03","fileNumber":"2026FL1143","shortTitle":"Government Records Classification Amendments","currentSubVersion":"3","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"SHEPHL","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shepherd, Lisa","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions related to the classification of certain government records.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends the definition of \"initial contact report\" for purposes of the Government Records Access and Management Act;<hr><ltbullet>classifies as public any record that documents a governmental entity's receipt or expenditure of funds, including:<hr><ltbullet1>a record related to a financial account, budget, voucher, or grant;<hr><ltbullet1>a financial report or general ledger; and<hr><ltbullet1>a record documenting compensation a governmental entity pays to a vendor;<hr><ltbullet>if properly classified by the governmental entity, makes private any portion of a record that reveals whether a taxpayer receives a specified property tax exemption, deferral, abatement, or other relief; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Christine R. Gilbert","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"GWELJWFJWE","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 13:10:11.323","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","act